else. The terms follow.

1. DEFINITIONS

   "Kariz" means everything in this repository at https://github.com/Erfan-XRay/Kariz and
   the release archives the Licensor publishes on its Releases page: the tunnel core, the
   web panel and its agent, the manager script, the documentation, the website and the
   design files.

   "Core" means the tunnel program and library (the `kariz` crate and binary), the Kariz
   tunnel protocol and wire format, and the Kariz configuration format.

   "Official Release" means a release archive published by the Licensor, with its checksum
   and signature.

   "Licensor" means Erfan-XRay, the owner of Kariz. "You" means the person or organization
   using Kariz.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   2.1 Read. You may read and study the source code in the public repository, review it for
       security, and report problems.

   2.2 Run. You may run unmodified Official Releases, or unmodified builds that You made
       yourself from a tagged version of the source, on servers that You own or administer,
       for any lawful purpose, commercial or not, free of charge, provided the Core runs as
       part of Kariz: started by the Kariz panel, its agent or its manager script, or from
       its own configuration files as documented. Using Kariz tunnels between Your own
       servers to run Your own services is running Kariz, and is allowed.

   2.3 Propose changes. You may fork the repository on GitHub, and keep a private working
       copy, only to prepare changes that You submit back to the Licensor, and only until
       they are accepted or dropped.

   2.4 Quote. You may quote short excerpts, with a link to the repository, in documentation,
       reviews and bug reports.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   3.1 Use the Core outside Kariz. You may not use the Core, or any part of it (its code,
       algorithms, protocol, wire format, configuration format, build outputs), in, with or
       inside any other program, panel, service, product, library, script or tunnel. You may
       not link, embed, wrap, bundle or call it from other software, and no other software
       may be made to manage, drive or orchestrate it.

   3.2 Copy or derive. You may not copy, reproduce, translate, port to another language,
       adapt or create anything derived from any part of Kariz, and You may not write
       another implementation that speaks the Kariz protocol or reads the Kariz
       configuration format.

   3.3 Distribute. You may not distribute, publish, mirror, sublicense, sell, rent or lend
       Kariz, or a modified, rebranded or repackaged version of it. You may not offer Kariz
       itself as a product or a hosted service.

   3.4 Modify for use. You may not run a modified version of Kariz, other than the private
       working copy of 2.3, and You may not remove or alter its notices, its name, its
       signatures, or the checks that verify Official Releases.

   3.5 Train on it. You may not use Kariz, or any part of it, to train or fine-tune a
       machine learning model, or put it in a dataset for that purpose.

   3.6 Use the name. You may not use the name "Kariz" or its logo for other software or for
       a modified version of this software.

   3.7 Reverse engineer. You may not reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Official
       Releases, except as far as the law allows despite this clause.

